{"version":"2026.10.11-r25","id":"Q27279547","formula":"C₇H₁₀O₅","hill":"C7H10O5","elements":["H","C","O"],"composition":{"C":7.0,"H":10.0,"O":5.0},"names":{"en":"Diethyl mesoxalate"},"descriptions":{"en":"Diethyl oxomalonate is the diethyl ester of mesoxalic acid (ketomalonic acid), the simplest oxodicarboxylic acid and thus the first member (n = 0) of a homologous series HOOC–CO–(CH2)n–COOH with the higher homologues oxalacetic acid (n = 1), α-ketoglutaric acid (n = 2) and α-ketoadipic acid (n = 3) (the latter a metabolite of the amino acid lysine). Diethyl oxomalonate reacts because of its highly polarized keto group as electrophile in addition reactions and is a highly active reactant in pericyclic reactions such as the Diels-Alder reactions, cycloadditions or ene reactions."},"fame":5,"pubchemCid":69105,"mass":174.15,"charge":0,"smiles":"CCOC(=O)C(=O)C(=O)OCC","inchikey":"DBKKFIIYQGGHJO-UHFFFAOYSA-N","iupac":"diethyl 2-oxopropanedioate","classes":[{"qid":"Q113145171","names":{"en":"type of chemical entity","ru":"тип химического объекта","uk":"тип хімічної сутності"}}],"structureInfo":{"kind":"molecule","source":"pubchem","ref":"69105","atoms":22,"license":"PubChem (NIH), public data"},"structure":{"kind":"molecule","atoms":[{"x":-1.943,"y":-0.321,"z":0.275,"el":"O"},{"x":2.265,"y":0.074,"z":0.177,"el":"O"},{"x":0.434,"y":1.752,"z":0.853,"el":"O"},{"x":-1.905,"y":1.716,"z":-0.841,"el":"O"},{"x":0.695,"y":-1.153,"z":-1.001,"el":"O"},{"x":-3.343,"y":-0.475,"z":0.026,"el":"C"},{"x":3.301,"y":-0.844,"z":-0.184,"el":"C"},{"x":-3.812,"y":-1.78,"z":0.634,"el":"C"},{"x":4.606,"y":-0.382,"z":0.428,"el":"C"},{"x":0.055,"y":0.826,"z":0.153,"el":"C"},{"x":-1.397,"y":0.806,"z":-0.217,"el":"C"},{"x":1.043,"y":-0.22,"z":-0.304,"el":"C"},{"x":-3.889,"y":0.361,"z":0.476,"el":"H"},{"x":-3.523,"y":-0.485,"z":-1.055,"el":"H"},{"x":3.05,"y":-1.843,"z":0.19,"el":"H"},{"x":3.395,"y":-0.879,"z":-1.275,"el":"H"},{"x":-4.881,"y":-1.931,"z":0.461,"el":"H"},{"x":-3.261,"y":-2.624,"z":0.206